# Google Drive API Integration Configuration
# 
# To enable Google Drive integration for slideshow and gallery images:
# 1. Copy this file to .env
# 2. Set up Google Cloud Console project and enable Google Drive API
# 3. Create an API key and add it below
# 4. Get your "galleries" folder ID and add it below
# 5. Make sure your folders are publicly accessible
#
# Google Cloud Console Setup:
# 1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/
# 2. Create a new project: "vineeth-photography-api"
# 3. Enable Google Drive API
# 4. Create API Key (restrict to Google Drive API and your domains)
#
# How to get the folder ID:
# 1. Open your "galleries" folder in Google Drive
# 2. Look at the URL: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/FOLDER_ID_HERE
# 3. Copy the FOLDER_ID_HERE part
#
# How to make folders publicly accessible:
# 1. Right-click your "galleries" folder → Share
# 2. Click "Change to anyone with the link"
# 3. Set permission to "Viewer"
# 4. Make sure all subfolders (Slideshow, Birds, etc.) inherit this permission
#
# Example:
# REACT_APP_GOOGLE_DRIVE_API_KEY=AIzaSyBxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# REACT_APP_GOOGLE_DRIVE_FOLDER_ID=1BxiMVs0XRA5nFMdKvBdBZjgmUUqptlbs74OgvE2upms

REACT_APP_GOOGLE_DRIVE_API_KEY=
REACT_APP_GOOGLE_DRIVE_FOLDER_ID=

# Note: If these environment variables are not set, 
# the app will automatically fall back to using local images